text.section:
A valid report or complaint means the local department has evaluated the information and allegations of the report or complaint and determined that the local department shall conduct an investigation, family assessment, or human trafficking assessment because the following elements are present:

The alleged victim child or children are under 18 years of age at the time of the complaint or report;


The alleged abuser is the alleged victim child's parent or other caretaker or, for purposes of abuse or neglect described in subdivision 4 of the definition of "abused or neglected child" in § 63.2-100, an intimate partner of such parent or caretaker;


The local department receiving the complaint or report has jurisdiction; and


The circumstances described allege suspected child abuse or neglect.
